  "pseudos": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "A cascade of failures in the Philippine power grid has exposed systemic rot. The outage of Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2, a privately-run generator, removed over 950 MW from the grid. This, combined with chronic issues from other aging plants and a surge in demand from the scorching summer heat, has pushed the system to its limit. Authorities, having already declared a red alert for the Visayas islands, have now ordered emergency load-shedding to prevent a catastrophic overload of the main transmission lines, forcing ordinary citizens to bear the cost of systemic neglect.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-2",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ]
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The crisis in the Visayas is not merely a technical glitch but a direct consequence of institutional failure. A single trip at a private power plant, Kepco SPC Power, triggered a massive 950 MW shortfall. This event was not isolated; it followed a pattern of generator failures and was exacerbated by a heatwave that overwhelmed the grid's fragile margins. The state's response—forced blackouts—highlights a lack of foresight and investment, making the population pay for the grid managers' inability to maintain reliable infrastructure.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-1",
          "why-2",
          "how-0",
