      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The red alert across the Philippine archipelago signals a profound failure of the power system. The immediate cause was a unit trip at Kepco SPC Power, wiping out critical capacity. However, the deeper issue is a grid plagued by aging infrastructure and poor management, now buckling under peak seasonal demand. The authorities' emergency order for load reduction is a stark admission of vulnerability, a measure that punishes consumers to protect a network they were assured was secure.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Outlaw",
